{
  "quest.147C1793BE9C2766.title": "&fBaBee Incubator",
  "quest.5C1E9A47B2D8F630.quest_desc": [
    "Your &2Planet Locator&r knows where a planet is. Now you need something to mine it.",
    "",
    "Craft the &aInterdimensional Laser&r and put your locators in it. It has six locator slots, and each one runs its own mining job.",
    "",
    "Every job draws its own power, from 500 RF/t on Fractoria up to 2,600 RF/t on Inferno and Asteroid, so six at once needs a large power supply. A job only runs while its planet is above the horizon, in a dimension where that planet is valid.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Each job has its own output slot and stops when that slot is full, so keep the laser emptied.",
  ],
  "quest.5010FC8F326DE471.title": "&dTinkering Table",
  "quest.74EEBED9D360FB82.title": "&aGrowing Budding Blocks",
  "quest.33AC3264C0AE8FF1.quest_desc": [
    "If you're looking to grow &bMob Seeds&r to convert into their loot, you'll need a few things to get started.",
    "",
    "The simplest way to do this is by making &aEmpty Soul Jars&r, and then filling them inside a &3Soul Extractor&r. This works by placing in something the mob might drop to extract the mob essence into the Soul Jar. Check JEI for recipes!",
    "",
    "You can also use the &aSoulium Dagger&r to kill mobs to fill the &2Soul Jars&r in your inventory.",
  ],
  "quest.085B40A50A0D4244.title": "&eMystical Agriculture",
  "quest.729B37ED4E838E59.title": "&aBigger Boxes",
  "quest.384287F30638679E.quest_desc": [
    "&dSupremium&r mob seeds close out the mob ladder. Wither Skeleton is the only one, and its essence crafts into Wither Skeleton Skulls.",
    "",
    "The Soul Jar step is the same as before, with 8 Wither Skeleton souls to a jar and four jars per seed.",
  ],
  "quest.1E340EC285631E9A.title": "&eEasy Villagers",
  "quest.3738420663297397.quest_desc": [
    "An empty &2Advanced Beehive&r left in the dark can pick up some unusual residents.",
    "",
    "Every 75 seconds at night, an Advanced Beehive with no bees inside has a 5% chance to take in a &dSkeletal Bee&r or a &5ZomBee&r. The space in front of the hive must be open, with no block light reaching it at all.",
    "",
    "Skeletal Bees need a Bone Block as their flower, and ZomBees use ordinary flowers. Their combs centrifuge into Bone Meal and Rotten Flesh.",
  ],
  "quest.42E45B47360C59F3.quest_desc": [
    "&2Essence Farmland&r is made by using an essence, from Inferium up to Insanium, on a piece of Farmland. These can also be crafted.",
    "",
    "An &aInferium&r crop drops more essence the higher the farmland tier under it, about half an essence more per tier, up to 3 or 4 on the top tiers. Other crops get a 10% chance of a second essence on any Essence Farmland, or 20% on the farmland that matches their own tier. Tier 6 crops get no bonus.",
  ],
  "quest.729B37ED4E838E59.quest_desc": [
    "Every box starts with 27 slots, and each tier adds 27 more, up to 108 at Tier 3. Storage slots also hold more per slot, from 64 items to 256, 1,024 and then 4,096, and from 32,000 mB of fluid up to 1,000,000 mB.",
    "",
    "Raise any of your apiary's boxes to Tier 1. A bigger Bee Box is the only way to run more bees in one apiary.",
    "",
    "Craft the next tier of a box, or use a &aBox Upgrade&r on one that is already placed to raise it where it stands. A box goes up one tier at a time, and Tier 3 costs a &2Nether Star&r.",
  ],
  "quest.2E56DB4CBFE2F37C.quest_desc": [
    "1 Imperium = 64 Inferium Essence",
  ],
  "quest.5133D15ADD337371.title": "&6Upgradeable Furnace",
  "quest.45F8CB4497591B10.title": "&cTier 3 &rMob Seeds",
  "quest.10B7437F3E412D26.quest_desc": [
    "To create an &6Ancient Bee&r, use a &aNetherite Block&r on a &2Diamond Bee&r to convert it over.",
    "",
    "This bee uses a &aNetherite Block&r as its flower, which is kind of expensive.",
  ],
  "quest.7695C03E7A574D93.title": "&bProsperity Shards",
  "quest.47893FC4BA520CE7.quest_desc": [
    "An &aIron Farm&r with a villager inside spawns and kills an iron golem every 4,800 ticks. Each golem drops 3 to 5 iron.",
  ],
  "quest.66477F0AB0AC2CDB.quest_desc": [
    "The &aCrafter&r automatically crafts a single recipe setup in its interface.",
  ],
  "task.0FB6B81D9E1E258E.title": "Blue Banded Bee Nests",
  "quest.385293121273C7FB.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Productivity Beta",
  "quest.611514BAC644DA7A.title": "&aTrader",
  "quest.2E9C4B70A1D6F385.title": "&cForeign Skies",
  "task.4C1919EBB6897E10.title": "Advanced Beehives",
  "quest.1DBAC590575ABA64.quest_desc": [
    "Budding ancient debris doesn't form a geode. It replaces a single netherrack block that isn't touching air, at most about once every six Nether chunks, so tunnel through solid netherrack to find it.",
    "",
    "Its clusters drop one shard each, with or without Fortune. The shards craft back into &2Ancient Debris&r, which makes a budding block a slow but endless netherite source.",
  ],
  "task.2307FBB6846EF266.title": "Resource Generation",
  "quest.207CED1C925F85C4.quest_desc": [
    "Once you have a &cRedstone Bee&r, breed it with a &aBlue Banded Bee&r to make a &9Lapis Bee&r!",
    "",
    "These are needed to make the Diamond Bee.",
  ],
  "quest.6EA5D8059A27679E.quest_desc": [
    "Past the &aNether Mining Portal&r are 128 layers of solid netherrack with nether ores spread through it, including &6Aeternium&r and Ancient Debris. Occultism's Iesnium is there too, but it only shows while you wear &2Otherworld Goggles&r and needs an &aInfused Pickaxe&r to mine.",
    "",
    "Like the Mining Portal it only works from the Overworld. Placed in the Nether it refuses to send you anywhere, so build it at home.",
  ],
  "quest.7AEC335123E441BA.quest_desc": [
    "&aTertium&r unlocks the third tier, and this is where seeds start replacing whole mining trips.",
    "",
    "Every tier grows at the same speed as wheat, so more essence means more plants. A &2Growth Accelerator&r adds extra growth ticks, but it skips the block right on top of it, so put it under the farmland, not directly under the crop.",
  ],
  "task.5A7D16167EA18581.title": "&dEnd &rNests",
  "quest.34AD046C45AE20CA.title": "&aBreeder",
  "quest.4506DB8F74B9C6A7.quest_desc": [
    "Two machines that run the altar recipes for you, with no pedestals to load.",
    "",
    "- &aInfusion Altarnator&r runs &2Infusion Altar&r recipes, seeds and augments included.",
    "- &aAwakening Altarnator&r runs &2Awakening Altar&r recipes.",
    "",
    "Both burn furnace fuel and take a &2Machine Upgrade&r like the other machines here.",
    "",
    "&7&oBuild these once you are crafting seeds in bulk&r",
  ],
  "quest.5133D15ADD337371.quest_desc": [
    "This is a furnace that takes a &aMachine Upgrade&r. It smelts anything a vanilla furnace can, at the same base speed, and a Supremium upgrade brings each smelt down from 200 ticks to 5.",
    "",
    "In JEI and in your inventory it is just called &aFurnace&r. Search &b@mysticalagriculture furnace&r to find it.",
  ],
  "task.75EC422F0D5A29CE.title": "Any &bTier 4 &rSeeds",
  "quest.6EDDB490A109A1E5.title": "&aFarmer",
  "quest.579FD80042103DEF.title": "&fSnow Nest",
  "quest.39214B204D3BEB2A.quest_desc": [
    "We all want our bees to produce more combs, and the speed upgrade just isn't enough.",
    "",
    "The &aUpgrade: Productivity Alpha&r is the first step towards the ultimate production hive. This upgrade increases the amount of combs produced in the hive by &a120%&r, and yes, you can install multiple to stack the effect.",
    "",
    "If you want to make these, you'll need a lot of &6Draconic Bees&r!",
  ],
  "quest.1A4F6C1AC9BD2F42.quest_desc": [
    "You can make &cRedstone Bees&r by breeding &aGlowing Bees&r with &2Chocolate Mining Bees&r.",
  ],
  "quest.1FA3F7A9AF119411.quest_desc": [
    "With &eApplied Energistics 2&r, the &aME Storage Interface&r can take the place of a Storage and send everything your bees make straight into your ME network, items and fluids alike.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aME Storage Interface&r and put it where a Storage would go. It needs power and a channel like any other ME device.",
    "",
    "Anything the network can't take falls through to your Storage boxes, and an apiary can only have one interface.",
  ],
  "quest.0D79C07499BF6E95.quest_desc": [
    "To create &6Awakened Supremium Essence&r, we'll need to create a new altar for the Awakening.",
    "",
    "Just like the &aInfusion Altar&r, place down the &6Awakening Altar&r first to show a guide on where to place the pedestals and vessels. To create the recipe, the altar will also need a redstone signal.",
    "",
    "Items for the recipe will be placed directly on the &6Awakening Pedestals&r. Each &6Essence Vessel&r holds one kind of essence, so fill the four with Air, Earth, Water and Fire Essence.",
  ],
  "quest.46D4262D31E94814.quest_desc": [
    "In Productive Bees, there are several ways to get all of the different bees. Some bees are more wild! These usually require a certain &2Nest&r, which you can learn more about in the Nest quest! There are also specific bees that &bcan only be fished up&r!",
    "",
    "One of the main methods of acquiring new bees is by &aBee Breeding&r. This is done just like vanilla breeding and requires you to give two bees a flower each to begin the process.",
    "",
    "In this mod, each bee will have a flower type that it likes to be able to breed. This can be seen in the tooltip for the bee when it is captured in a &aBee Cage&r. You can also use JEI to check the recipes for the bee as well.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Specific bees can also be &6Converted&r by feeding the bee a specific block. For example, feeding a vanilla bee &cTNT&r will convert it into a CreeBee. This is also something you can see in JEI!",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Lastly, Bees can also be crafted in different ways. Usually this is done when you want to make a specific bee using a mod's crafting mechanics like using altars to craft it.",
    "",
    "Obtaining bee spawn eggs can be done using genes, and is explained in the Gene quest.",
  ],
  "quest.142D8B60C2D3B81D.quest_desc": [
    "The &aCollector&r picks up dropped items inside a box around it. The offset buttons in its menu shift that box up to 10 blocks along each axis, and a &2Radius Increase Module&r makes it larger. It has no item filter, so it keeps everything that drops in range.",
    "",
    "Experience pickup starts switched off. Turn it on in the Collector's screen and it banks the experience too, and you can store or withdraw levels from the same screen.",
  ],
  "quest.603BAFEF92DA275E.quest_desc": [
    "With the help of &2Inferium Ingots&r and &aInferium Gemstones&r, we can upgrade Diamond armor into Inferium armor, which lasts longer and adds an armor point on the boots.",
    "",
    "Armor from this mod can be upgraded using the &aTinkering Table&r using &dAugments&r.",
  ],
  "quest.4C466A8B9C76C637.quest_desc": [
    "When given Honey Treats, these can be used to lure in Blue Banded Bees.",
  ],
  "task.0657D2B7110B89A9.title": "Any Bee Cage",
  "quest.2E9C4B70A1D6F385.quest_desc": [
    "Two planets never show over the Overworld, so the laser has to travel.",
    "",
    "- &cAsteroid&r (level 8) hangs in the &5End&r sky and streams raw ores. Iridium, boron and titanium come up most often, then tin, lead, nickel, uranium, aluminum and coal, with copper, gold, redstone, iron, silver and platinum behind them.",
    "- &5Cindrath&r (level 10) shows over the &dEnd&r as well, with magma, red sand and the odd block of obsidian.",
    "",
    "Lock your locators in the &5End&r, where both are drawn. A laser for either one also works in the &cNether&r, though no planets show under its roof. Asteroid is the slowest job in the laser, one item every 400 ticks at 2,600 RF/t.",
  ],
  "quest.562421EC1575F837.title": "&fIron Bees",
  "quest.20ED9BF15D0E7F54.title": "&6Centrifuge Tier 3",
  "quest.6A2F8E14C7B5D093.quest_desc": [
    "Four planets hang over the Overworld.",
    "",
    "- &aFractoria&r (level 8) is the budget option, a steady drip of stone, cobblestone, basalt and blackstone.",
    "- &2Submerged&r (level 12) pays out sand, gravel and prismarine.",
    "- &aCrystalore&r (level 12) is the one you build the tower for. Diamonds, emeralds, lapis, quartz, amethyst, and even more &dDimensional Shards&r.",
    "- &6Inferno&r (level 12) brings Nether spoils home, mostly quartz, glowstone dust and certus quartz, with netherrack, raw gold, sulfur and gravel behind them. &2Ancient Debris&r comes up about once in 126 rolls and &aNetherite Scrap&r about once in 377.",
  ],
  "quest.388EAAF7CFA6535F.quest_desc": [
    "You can catch yourself a &aGold Bee&r by using a &2Nether Gold Nest&r in the Nether, or by breeding a Mason Bee and a Crystalline Bee.",
  ],
  "quest.7AEC335123E441BA.title": "&cTier 3 &rSeeds",
  "quest.5CE002C1C1142CD1.title": "&fMaking &aCustom Seeds",
  "quest.6EDDB490A109A1E5.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFarmer&r simulates crop growth within one block. Give it a seed, the farmland that seed needs and some furnace fuel, and it grows and harvests that seed inside the machine.",
  ],
  "quest.12663AA928D0E094.quest_desc": [
    "Two traits can be trained instead of bred, and both need a &aLead&r.",
    "",
    "- &aWeather Tolerance&r: leave a bee leashed outside through rain or a thunderstorm and it can learn to work in that weather.",
    "- &aBehavior&r: leash a Diurnal bee outside at night for a chance to turn it Nocturnal, then leash that bee through the day for a chance at Metaturnal.",
    "",
    "A bee kept out in conditions it isn't used to takes damage while it adjusts. Stay close and heal it with &aHoney Treats&r. Each treat also has a small chance to calm its Temper by one step.",
  ],
  "task.76E4EFD2BC3FA68E.title": "Any Gem &aGeOre Shard&r",
  "quest.45F8CB4497591B10.quest_desc": [
    "Mob seeds at &aTertium&r. Same rule as the earlier ones, so you need a &aSoulium Seed Base&r and four filled &2Soul Jars&r of the mob you are after.",
    "",
    "Growing the drops beats building the farm. No spawner, no lighting, no mob cap to argue with.",
  ],
  "quest.1C742A1E7C1F1059.quest_desc": [
    "Killing the &cEnder Dragon&r unlocks the &aEnd Mining Portal&r recipe in the &2FTB Fabricator&r.",
    "",
    "This checks the Free the End advancement, so a dragon killed before this point still counts if anyone on your team has it.",
  ],
  "quest.12663AA928D0E094.title": "&aTraining Your Bees",
  "quest.16C668B00B581A9C.quest_desc": [
    "There are many types of bees in the world, but these can be broken down into two main categories.",
    "",
    "The first type you'll encounter are called &aSolitary Bees&r. These types of bees are usually spawned from &2Nests&r, which can be crafted. These bees &bdo not create any items&r, and as such can only live in their preferred nests. They are mainly used for breeding new types of bees!",
    "",
    "Examples of Solitary Bees: Reed, Blue Banded, Carpenter",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The second type of bee we'll just call &eProductive Bees&r, because they actually produce something and mostly live in your Advanced Beehives.",
    "",
    "These bees are not found in the wild as often, and are mostly made from various methods like &aBee Breeding&r or &bBee Conversion&r. Some bees are also crafted by crafting their spawn eggs!",
    "",
    "Examples of Productive Bees: Iron, Diamond, Sugarbag",
  ],
  "quest.39214B204D3BEB2A.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Productivity Alpha",
  "quest.230E34A0E4A4C014.title": "&fBeehives to &aBeehomes",
  "quest.5F6C674205F3D666.title": "&dEnd &rNests",
  "quest.6EA5D8059A27679E.title": "&cNether Mining",
  "task.62ED0EC3C8534504.title": "&eGeOre",
  "quest.7FC24DE55428724A.quest_desc": [
    "If you're looking to automate capturing Bees, the &aCatcher&r is the machine for you!",
    "",
    "It will need some Bee Cages stored to capture the bees in, and can also be upgraded to filter what it catches. You can also increase its range using the Range Upgrade!",
  ],
  "quest.7FC24DE55428724A.title": "&fAuto-Catching Bees",
  "quest.34AD046C45AE20CA.quest_desc": [
    "Put two villagers and some food in a &aBreeder&r and it makes a new villager every 1,200 ticks.",
    "",
    "The &2Converter&r takes a villager, a golden apple and a weakness potion. It turns the villager into a zombie villager and cures it again over 6,180 ticks, and the cure discount is shared by every player.",
  ],
  "quest.2AF9753B396F7625.title": "&dMaster Infusion Crystal",
  "quest.7885F26DBF1E2E8F.quest_desc": [
    "Traits move from bee to bee in three ways.",
    "",
    "- &aBreeding&r: the baby rolls each of Productivity, Endurance, Behavior and Weather Tolerance between its two parents' levels, never below its own type's default, and takes the calmer Temper.",
    "- &aConversion&r: a converted bee keeps the traits it had, except where the new type's default is better.",
    "- &aGene treats&r: each gene on a Honey Treat has a chance equal to its purity to take hold when the bee eats it.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Combining two samples of the same gene raises its purity, and so does adding more of that gene to a treat, up to 100%.",
    "",
    "The &aBaBee Incubator&r only reads the type gene when it makes a spawn egg. Its purity is the chance that the egg converts, and a failure still uses up both the egg and the treat, so get the type gene to 100% first.",
  ],
  "quest.51B5EE931AC1B86E.quest_desc": [
    "The Nests can only be placed in the &cNether&r to lure in bees.",
    "",
    "- &aGlowstone Nest&r lure in Glowing Bees when given Glowstone Dust.",
    "",
    "- &aSoul Sand Nests&r lure in Ghostly Bees when given Ghast Tears.",
    "",
    "- &aQuartz Nests&r lure in Crystalline Bees when given Nether Quartz.",
    "",
    "- &aNether Gold Nests&r lure in Gold Bees when given Gold Ingots.",
    "",
    "- &aNether Brick Nests&r lure in Magmatic Bees when given Magma Cream.",
  ],
  "quest.5FB291FDE43A727F.title": "&aHoney &rTreats",
  "quest.384287F30638679E.title": "&dTier 5 &rMob Seeds",
  "quest.388EAAF7CFA6535F.title": "&6Gold Bees",
  "quest.30053CAD8FABA638.quest_desc": [
    "These Nests lure bees in any Overworld biome.",
    "",
    "The &aStone Nest&r can be used to lure in Mason or Digger bees when given Honey Treats.",
    "",
    "The &aDirt Nest&r lures in Chocolate Mining, Ashy Mining, and Leafcutter bees when given Honey Treats.",
  ],
  "quest.1CFEC4265CAAA0D8.quest_desc": [
    "&bWatering Cans&r are pretty simple. Fill one by using it on a water source, then hold use while looking at your crops to water the area around them. You can also sneak and use a filled can while looking into the air to switch it on, and it waters wherever you look while you hold it.",
    "",
    "The higher the tier, the more area that it covers. This pack lets fake players use watering cans, so a &2Clicker&r from &eJust Dire Things&r can work one for you.",
  ],
  "quest.0B7E3C58D19A46F2.quest_desc": [
    "Every planet has a minimum &blaser level&r, and the laser's level is the number of complete tower layers under it, up to &a12&r.",
    "",
    "A layer is a full 3 by 3 of &aDimensional Stone&r centered under the laser, plus one &2Dimensional Stone Bricks&r block at each corner, two blocks out diagonally from the center. A layer missing any block ends the count there.",
    "",
    "Each layer costs 25 &2Dimensional Shards&r: 9 for the stone in the center and 16 for the four corner bricks. Budget 200 shards for the starter level-8 tower, or 300 for all 12 layers, before the laser and locator.",
  ],
  "quest.645887524E6E08C2.quest_desc": [
    "The &aHeated Centrifuge&r is the fastest centrifuge in &eProductive Bees&r. It runs three times faster than the Powered Centrifuge and uses three times the power.",
    "",
    "It also takes &2Comb Blocks&r as well as single combs, and it will void any Wax it produces.",
  ],
  "quest.208A53545D649C8D.quest_desc": [
    "Machines from this mod can be upgraded using &aMachine Upgrades&r!",
    "",
    "Each tier makes the machine faster and lets it hold more fuel, but it also burns fuel faster, and on the Harvester and Fertilizer it widens the area. Expand the upgrade's tooltip to see its exact numbers.",
  ],
  "task.3B199396B2DF554D.title": "&cNether &rNests",
  "quest.234A09F196E91BDD.title": "&6Resource Generation",
  "quest.2436337445AD0E07.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Block Upgrade&r will convert a hive to produce &aComb Blocks&r instead of regular Combs.",
    "",
    "This is a massive upgrade for production!",
  ],
  "quest.60EBD67EDCE669DD.quest_desc": [
    "&dSupremium&r, the top of the normal ladder.",
    "",
    "Everything past this point is Tier 6, and a Tier 6 crop only grows with its &2Crux&r under the farmland. These are the last seeds that grow on farmland alone.",
  ],
  "quest.385293121273C7FB.quest_desc": [
    "Using 4 Alpha Upgrades and some &dNether Stars&r, we can create the next tier of productivity upgrades: &6Upgrade: Productivity Beta&r.",
    "",
    "This increases the production of the hive by 150% each. We need these to make the next tier!",
  ],
  "quest.2D2EC0BCFF1DA68C.title": "&fBee Stats",
  "quest.65337DD4E5CABB58.title": "&aGenesis Chamber",
  "quest.0B7E3C58D19A46F2.title": "&aRaising the Tower",
  "quest.30AB20CB8C626A7C.title": "&aOre Infuser",
  "quest.30053CAD8FABA638.title": "&fStone \\&\\ Dirt Nests",
  "quest.68A9B5BD25E86D75.quest_subtitle": "Tier 3",
  "quest.4FD329857906DB24.quest_desc": [
    "The same arrangement with a &5Dragon Egg Crux&r underneath.",
    "",
    "Minecraft hands out exactly one dragon egg. This hands out as many as you have patience for.",
  ],
  "quest.42E45B47360C59F3.title": "&fUnderstanding &2Essence Farmland",
  "task.636E5A09D2D8BB32.title": "Any &aTier 1&r apiary box or Box Upgrade",
  "quest.0A1FDABEAAA0723B.quest_desc": [
    "Probably one of the best upgrades for servers, the &aSimulator Upgrade&r prevents Bees inside of the hive from needing to leave.",
    "",
    "They will still need their flowering item or block to create combs. If this upgrade is installed, the flowering block or feeding slab must be placed one block down from the front of the Hive, as shown in the image below.",
    "",
    "{image:ftb:textures/quests/productivebees/advancedbeehivesim.png width:125 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.272C00767FDBD64F.title": "&fReed Nest",
  "quest.2F74CE4932170B99.title": "&fSpruce Nest",
  "quest.13448A305B57016A.quest_desc": [
    "If you're looking to upgrade your gear, &aInferium Gear&r lasts longer and digs faster than Diamond, though in this pack its swords and axes hit slightly softer. There are also great new tools like &aScythes&r and &2Sickles&r that provide an AoE harvesting effect!",
    "",
    "These tools can also be upgraded using &dAugments&r in a Tinkering Table.",
  ],
  "quest.579FD80042103DEF.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSnow Nest&r must be placed in a snowy biome to lure in bees.",
    "",
    "When given Honey Treats, these will lure in Sweat bees.",
  ],
  "quest.290D1B111FD24B32.quest_desc": [
    "To make &dDiamond Bees&r, you'll need to have captured an &aEnder Bee&r using an End Stone Nest in the End. You can breed one of the Ender Bees with a &9Lapis Bee&r to make the &dDiamond Bee&r!",
  ],
  "quest.0D92EFDB73114B0C.quest_desc": [
    "With &2Prudentium&r, you now have access to make &bMob Seeds&r.",
    "",
    "Unlike most of the regular seeds, these require a &2Soulium Seed Base&r to create, as well as filled &aSoul Jars&r of the desired mob essence.",
  ],
  "quest.1E340EC285631E9A.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak and interact with a villager to pick it up as an item. &eEasy Villagers&r blocks hold villagers and run one job with them inside a single block.",
  ],
  "quest.586E18023A595A6C.title": "&eProductive Bees",
  "task.19FB3879C5AE09BA.title": "Any &dTier 5 &rMob Seeds",
  "quest.7C9CABB75B422A4A.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Awakening Altar&r is where a &2Supremium Block&r gets Awakened! Craft the &aAwakened Supremium Block&r back down to get the essence.",
    "",
    "Awakened Supremium is the top tier of &eMystical Agriculture&r gear, and Awakened gear holds two augments instead of one.",
  ],
  "task.10797452061EB3E6.title": "Any &aTier 1 &rSeeds",
  "quest.197CF94F783E59DF.quest_desc": [
    "Each &aUpgrade: Speed&r cuts 15% off the time bees spend inside the hive, or off a machine's processing time. You can also place multiple in one machine!",
    "",
    "These can also be placed in more than just Beehives. Try it in your Centrifuges, Breeding Chambers, and more!",
  ],
  "task.2566CE0AC0925C71.title": "Any &2Tier 2 &rMob Seeds",
  "quest.792BD1143635482C.title": "&fGravel \\&\\ Sand Nests",
  "quest.74EEBED9D360FB82.quest_desc": [
    "Found a geode far from home? Grow your own budding block instead of moving there. The &eEnergized Power&r &2Crystal Growth Chamber&r turns GeOre blocks into their budding block.",
    "",
    "Each attempt takes 32,000 ticks, about 27 minutes before speed upgrades, and only one in four succeeds, so start one early.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Crystal Growth Chamber\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"6A59069E389CBA24\", \"page\": 1}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Crystal Growth Chamber Quest\"}}]",
  ],
  "quest.5574D291E6E69013.title": "&2Prudentium Essence",
  "quest.7123022757E50A70.quest_subtitle": "Tier 6",
  "quest.65337DD4E5CABB58.quest_desc": [
    "The &aGenesis Chamber&r spawns mobs in a 5x5 area around it and burns fuel to do it. Put a spawn egg in its egg slot to choose the mob. The egg is never used up.",
    "",
    "The &aGenesis Infuser&r soaks coal and charcoal in experience. Infused coal burns eight times longer, so it keeps a chamber running far longer per item.",
  ],
  "task.1E4BBCF77E4AE460.title": "Expansion Box",
  "quest.0241EAE68EA53595.title": "&fNest Spawning",
  "quest.736EF0026F658DA7.quest_desc": [
    "&2Prudentium&r opens the second rung, with seeds such as Coal, Amethyst, Dye and Nether.",
    "",
    "Same infusion recipe as before, one tier up on the essence. Craft the ones you are short of rather than working through the whole list.",
  ],
  "quest.3C4D8CB7120C8219.quest_desc": [
    "Beyond the &aEnd Mining Portal&r are 128 layers of solid end stone, with end ores spread through it, including &6Aurichalcum&r and Niobium.",
    "",
    "It only works from the Overworld, the same as the other two.",
    "",
    "The &dUnstable Portal Fluid&r it takes comes from &eJust Dire Things&r, so get that running before you gather everything else.",
  ],
  "quest.09BC75B655BDC624.title": "&aUpgrade&r: BaBee",
  "quest.2EBDE5767588B43C.title": "&6Cognizant Dust",
  "quest.1C742A1E7C1F1059.title": "&5Free the End",
  "quest.3F8B2D61C4A97E05.quest_desc": [
    "You can see the planets moving across the sky without a telescope. A &aSpyglass&r lets you identify one and bind a &2Planet Locator&r to it.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aSpyglass&r and a &2Planet Locator&r, hold the locator in your &boff-hand&r, and scan the sky through the spyglass. Spot a planet and the locator locks onto it.",
    "",
    "Planets only show in the dimensions they belong to, and two of them never appear over the Overworld. A locator keeps the first planet it finds, so make one locator per planet you care about.",
  ],
  "quest.2315DBE189D330DA.quest_desc": [
    "Those Draconic Bees have been putting in a lot of work, but it's all about to pay off.",
    "",
    "This is the ultimate upgrade for a hive, the &6Upgrade: Productivity Omega&r. This increases productivity by 260% each, and also acts as a Simulator Upgrade AND as a Block Upgrade. Instead of producing just regular combs, you'll get comb blocks instead.",
    "",
    "Pro Tip: 4 Productivity Upgrades are better than using speed upgrades at all!",
  ],
  "quest.6A2F8E14C7B5D093.title": "&bOverworld Skies",
  "quest.1A314C332514AF39.title": "&aInfuser",
  "quest.73F82078E2BC4DA5.quest_desc": [
    "This is where the upgrades start to get fun!",
    "",
    "The &6Upgrade: Productivity Gamma&r increases the production of the hive by 200%, AND it also acts as a &aSimulator Upgrade&r.",
    "",
    "Unlike the previous upgrades, you won't need a Simulator Upgrade installed, which allows you to place another one of the upgrades in it instead!",
  ],
  "quest.3490E1E29396D066.title": "&aTier 1 &rSeeds",
  "quest.1003322F319665FF.quest_desc": [
    "Killing a &cWither&r after your team has built the &aFTB Skyline&r unlocks the &2Nether Mining Portal&r recipe in the FTB Fabricator.",
    "",
    "Only a kill made after this quest opens counts, so a Wither you fought before building the Skyline does not.",
  ],
  "quest.4B38B74EA8E13AAE.quest_desc": [
    "&eMob Flow Utilities&r is a kit for mob farms. Use a &aGloom Spore&r on dirt or grass to turn a 5x5 area into &2Dark Dirt&r. Every 20 ticks each Dark Dirt block tries to spawn a monster from the biome's list, as long as the light level above it is 0.",
    "",
    "Dark Dirt that can see the sky in daylight turns back into plain dirt, so build the farm under a roof. A &2Glimmer Sprout&r makes &aGlimmer Grass&r the same way. It spawns the biome's animals instead and needs a light level of 7 or more.",
    "",
    "Either block stops spawning while 12 of its mobs are within 8 blocks of it, so keep the floor cleared. The spore and sprout take an &2XP Fluid Bucket&r from &eJust Dire Things&r.",
  ],
  "quest.73F82078E2BC4DA5.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Productivity Gamma",
  "task.62AEAB0BA2360576.title": "Any &cTier 3 &rSeeds",
  "quest.2AE9ADF578ABEA11.quest_subtitle": "Tier 5",
  "quest.142D8B60C2D3B81D.title": "&aCollector",
  "quest.458B3C345767E296.quest_desc": [
    "Tier six, and the first crop that will not grow on its own. Put a &aNether Star Crux&r under the farmland, two blocks below the crop, or nothing happens.",
    "",
    "A wither for every star stops being the plan. This is the plan.",
  ],
  "quest.736EF0026F658DA7.title": "&2Tier 2 &rSeeds",
  "quest.2AE9ADF578ABEA11.quest_desc": [
    "1 Supremium = 256 Inferium Essence",
  ],
  "quest.085B40A50A0D4244.quest_subtitle": "Tier 1",
  "quest.780FEFE9F073543B.quest_subtitle": "Colonies that make metal",
  "task.2C1245371800E1E7.title": "Bee Types",
  "quest.702D49883F3011DE.title": "&aSeed Reprocessor",
  "quest.4FD329857906DB24.title": "&5Dragon Egg Seeds",
  "quest.2E56DB4CBFE2F37C.quest_subtitle": "Tier 4",
  "quest.234A09F196E91BDD.quest_desc": [
    "This chapter covers the mods that turn one setup into a steady supply of resources, from bees and magical crops to geodes, mob farms, villagers, planet lasers and the mining dimensions. Pick whichever covers what you're short on.",
  ],
  "quest.0EBA58B7FD2AF36D.quest_desc": [
    "Certain materials are difficult to farm or create, specifically things like &dDragon's Breath&r.",
    "",
    "That's where the &aExtractor&r comes in! This is a simple machine that allows you to create mini structures to extract items from the blocks around them. This can be something as simple as a cobblestone generator using lava and water, or farming snowballs from mini snowmen!",
    "",
    "Note that some recipes require certain blocks to be placed in a specific direction around the &aExtractor&r.",
    "",
    "&7&oThe Extractor makes pointed dripstone too, from a dripstone block and water. JEI shows the layout.&r",
  ],
  "quest.5574D291E6E69013.quest_subtitle": "Tier 2",
  "quest.5F6C674205F3D666.quest_desc": [
    "These Nests will only lure bees when placed in the End.",
    "",
    "- &aEnd Stone Nests&r lure in Ender Bees when given Popped Chorus Fruit. These bees will randomly teleport!",
    "",
    "- &aObsidian Nests&r lure in Draconic Bees when given Dragon's Breath.",
  ],
  "quest.780FEFE9F073543B.title": "&eNautec&r Bacteria",
  "quest.3C4D8CB7120C8219.title": "&dEnd Mining",
  "quest.085B40A50A0D4244.quest_desc": [
    "&eMystical Agriculture&r allows you to create plants of pretty much every resource, including mobs. If you are the farming type and never want to worry about resources again, Mystical Ag is the way to go.",
    "",
    "To start your adventure, you'll need to collect &aInferium Essence&r. You can fish it up or mine the ore.",
    "",
    "Once you have at least 8, you can make your first &aInferium Seed&r to start growing it!",
  ],
  "task.683638FC21EA1713.title": "Any &dTier 5 &rSeeds",
  "quest.6451DEA471C5FF6F.quest_desc": [
    "A &aController&r runs up to 25 &2Damage Pads&r within 8 blocks of it. Use the &aPad Wrench&r on the Controller to select it, then on each pad to link it.",
    "",
    "&aFans&r and &2Flow Pads&r push mobs onto the pads, so the whole farm runs without you swinging a sword.",
  ],
  "quest.6AB0C61A12C417F2.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSoulium Spawner&r spends mob essence to spawn the mob itself; so Zombie Essence spawns Zombies with the odd Husk or Zombie Villager. Each spawn costs 12 to 32 essence depending on the mob.",
    "",
    "Mobs appear in the 7x7 area around the spawner, on the same y-level, and essence is only used when a mob has room to appear.",
    "",
    "A redstone signal pauses it.",
  ],
  "task.1F6A4C82E9B3D570.title": "Planet Locators",
  "quest.586E18023A595A6C.quest_desc": [
    "Plain honey only goes so far. With &eProductive Bees&r, bees can bring back materials like Raw Iron and Diamonds instead.",
    "",
    "You'll need some ordinary bees first. Wild &2Bee Nests&r hang from trees in plains, meadows, forests and cherry groves. Without Silk Touch, breaking a nest drops nothing and lets the bees out angry, so harvest it where it hangs.",
    "",
    "Once a nest is full of honey, use Shears or a Glass Bottle on it. Keep a lit campfire up to five blocks under the nest first, or the bees inside come out angry.",
    "",
    "Catch a bee in a &2Bee Cage&r and &dThe Apiarist&r will start trading with you. You can find them in plains, meadow and savanna villages, selling a few Bee Spawn Eggs along with Honey Treats and nests.",
  ],
  "quest.1A314C332514AF39.quest_desc": [
    "The &aInfuser&r automatically infuses essences together into higher-tier essences when provided with a &dMaster Infusion Crystal&r.",
    "",
    "Click the small square below the tier you'd like it to send to the output slot to improve your automation.",
  ],
  "quest.0C259021A652EFCE.quest_desc": [
    "&eMystical Agriculture&r has its own block for speeding up crops, the &aGrowth Accelerator&r. About every 10 seconds, each one gives an extra growth tick to the first crop it finds above it.",
    "",
    "An accelerator skips the block right on top of it, so it goes under the farmland. Stack them in a column and every accelerator that can reach the crop adds its own ticks. Higher tiers do not tick faster. They only have a longer range, from 9 blocks for Inferium up to 54 for Awakened Supremium.",
    "",
    "For example, a tower of 18 Prudentium Growth Accelerators grows crops no faster than 9 Inferium stacked on top of 9 Prudentium. The higher tier only buys the extra reach.",
  ],
  "quest.230E34A0E4A4C014.quest_desc": [
    "Harvesting Honeycombs and Honey Bottles by hand is exhausting. And who actually uses the campfire trick? Just get the sting over with, you know?",
    "",
    "By making an &aAdvanced Beehive&r, you no longer need to manually harvest anymore. Bees will leave their products inside of these new homes to be easily collected!",
    "",
    "These can also be upgraded to hold up to 5 bees by placing an &2Expansion Box&r against any side except the front. Definitely worth upgrading!",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&aAdvanced Beehives&r will still require the bee's preferred flower nearby for them to create any type of resource. These can be seen in &eJEI&r!",
    "",
    "If you have multiple types of bees living in one hive, make sure to check out the &aFeeding Slab&r to keep your area tidy! This block allows you to place in several types of flowers or blocks in a single blockspace.",
  ],
  "quest.0D92EFDB73114B0C.title": "&2Tier 2 &rMob Seeds",
  "quest.2AF9753B396F7625.quest_desc": [
    "In this pack the &aMaster Infusion Crystal&r needs &2Insanium Essence&r rather than Supremium, so it comes after your first Insanium.",
    "",
    "It works as every tier's crystal at once and never breaks!",
  ],
  "quest.2BCDA4C64936EBE2.quest_desc": [
    "Quartz geodes generate in both the Overworld and the Nether. Diamond geodes show up about once every 330 chunks and emerald about once every 420.",
    "",
    "Each diamond shard is worth a whole diamond, so one budding diamond block pays for itself quickly.",
  ],
  "quest.1FA3F7A9AF119411.title": "&aME Storage Interface",
  "quest.30AB20CB8C626A7C.quest_desc": [
    "Ore goes back into stone in the &aOre Infuser&r. Give it Stone, Deepslate or Netherrack plus resource essence and it makes the matching ore block. The amount of essence varies depending on the ore it is infusing.",
  ],
  "quest.207CED1C925F85C4.title": "&9Lapis Bees",
  "quest.72D582D05DC9C7A2.quest_desc": [
    "&2Oak Nests&r can be crafted or found in the overworld in Oak trees.",
    "",
    "Giving them a Honey Treat will lure in either a Yellow or Green Carpenter Bee.",
  ],
  "quest.47893FC4BA520CE7.title": "&aIron Farm",
  "quest.77914AB759F51A62.quest_desc": [
    "While regular Honey Combs are needed as crafting materials, you are going to get lots of different types of combs, and most of them will need to be processed in a &aCentrifuge&r to make items out of them.",
    "",
    "When this machine processes the combs, it creates &aWax&r, some kind of useful item, and usually some kind of &2Honey&r. The easiest way to make use of the liquid honey is to send it into a &6Bottler&r to create Honey Bottles for you!",
    "",
    "The Centrifuge can also be upgraded into a &aPowered Centrifuge&r, which works faster at the cost of power. These can also accept &aSpeed Upgrades&r!",
  ],
  "quest.7C9CABB75B422A4A.quest_subtitle": "Awakened Tier",
  "task.5AF37B4A61876A3E.title": "Any &cTier 3 &rMob Seeds",
  "quest.5C1E9A47B2D8F630.title": "&dThe Interdimensional Laser",
  "task.473509F84E9C3147.title": "Nest Spawning",
  "quest.7CB0AFF443CB39DA.title": "&dMystical Enchanting",
  "quest.0D79C07499BF6E95.title": "&fAwakening Altar",
  "quest.2EBDE5767588B43C.quest_desc": [
    "To create &6Awakened Supremium&r, we'll need a dust that only drops from the &5Ender Dragon&r or the &dWither&r.",
    "",
    "This is called &6Cognizant Dust&r, and will only drop when they are slain with a Mystical Agriculture weapon enchanted with &dMystical Enlightenment&r.",
    "",
    "&dThe Jewler&r sells a &2Mystical Enlightenment&r book, one per player. You find the Jewler at taverns, and the shop opens once you have crafted a &2Jewelcrafting Station&r.",
  ],
  "quest.7123022757E50A70.title": "&5Insanium Essence",
  "quest.2E56DB4CBFE2F37C.title": "&bImperium Essence",
  "quest.358D66AB9176F05F.quest_desc": [
    "A XyCraft &aExtractor&r working on a budding GeOre block, with water beside it, produces one shard of that type every 1,200 ticks.",
    "",
    "It works on any budding block, including the ones you grow in a Crystal Growth Chamber.",
  ],
  "quest.37733B382007E7FA.title": "&6Modded Bees",
  "quest.67F07FBB50AB431F.quest_desc": [
    "&eApothic Spawners&r lets you move and upgrade &2Monster Spawners&r to build your own mob farms. To move a spawner, break it with a Silk Touch pickaxe, which costs the pickaxe 100 durability.",
    "",
    "Use a spawn egg on a spawner to change it to that mob.",
    "",
    "[\"Exploding a spawner will drop \", {\"text\": \"Spawner Chains\", \"color\": \"dark_green\"}, \" which are used to craft upgrades that can be applied to your spawners, improving their abilities. You'll require a more \", {\"text\": \"Advanced Enchantment Setup\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"00A7C1FE54F86429\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Apothic Enchanting Quest\"}}, \" to make more advanced spawner upgrades.\"]",
    "",
    "To learn more about which items to use, check the recipes in &eJEI&r for a spawner.",
  ],
  "quest.2BCDA4C64936EBE2.title": "&bGem GeOres",
  "quest.51729919E9A33049.quest_desc": [
    "Do you have a bee that has a high &aProductivity&r stat? Would you like all of your bees to have that stat?",
    "",
    "These specific stats, including the type of bee that it is, can be extracted from a bee as &6Genes&r. Let's talk about how to get them first!",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The easiest way is an &aUpgrade: Pokey pokey gene sampler&r in an Advanced Beehive. Each time an adult bee leaves after dropping off honey, every sampler installed adds a 5% chance that it gives up one random gene at 1 to 4% purity. Those samples pile up, so keep them in a &aGene Indexer&r.",
    "",
    "The Indexer merges matching genes on its own as they go in, adding their purity together up to 100%. A gene's purity is the chance it takes hold when you use it, so the higher the better, and a 100% gene never fails.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The other way costs you the bee. Put Glass Bottles in a &2Bottler&r, place a piston facing down two blocks above it, and fire the piston while an adult bee is in the space between them. The bee dies and leaves &2Squashed Bee Material&r.",
    "",
    "A &2Centrifuge&r breaks that down into one gene for each of the bee's traits plus its type, at much higher purity than the sampler gives.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "To use a gene, infuse it into a &2Honey Treat&r and feed the treat to a bee. You can also put the treat in the bottom slot of a &2BaBee Incubator&r with a caged bee in the left slot. Each gene on the treat takes hold with a chance equal to its purity, and the treat is used up either way.",
    "",
    "A treat carrying a bee type gene can't be fed to a bee. Put it in the Incubator with an egg instead to turn the egg into that bee's spawn egg. The type gene's purity is the chance it works.",
  ],
  "quest.10AE11528D94EB0E.title": "&aMystical Machines",
  "quest.1D4A7C29E5B30F16.title": "&eDimensional Resources",
  "quest.4C466A8B9C76C637.title": "&fBlue Banded Bee Nests",
  "task.5CF6E53B06825D6C.title": "Any Common &aGeOre Shard&r",
  "quest.46D4262D31E94814.title": "&fGetting Bees",
  "quest.272C00767FDBD64F.quest_desc": [
    "While &aReed Nests&r can be placed in any Overworld biome, they can only be found where sugarcane grows!",
    "",
    "When given Honey Treats, these will lure in Reed and Mason bees.",
  ],
  "quest.77914AB759F51A62.title": "&fUseful Machines",
  "quest.7C9CABB75B422A4A.title": "&6Awakened Essence",
  "quest.63E02402233F6865.title": "&aEasy Breeding&r!",
  "quest.68A9B5BD25E86D75.quest_desc": [
    "1 Tertium = 16 Inferium Essence",
  ],
  "quest.645887524E6E08C2.title": "&fHeated Centrifuge",
  "task.48BB22683A4C50AD.title": "&aInferium &rGear",
  "task.6F72448CD3FD5163.title": "How To Get Bees!",
  "quest.3490E1E29396D066.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 1 is your first set of resource seeds, with crops for Stone, Dirt, Wood, Ice and Deepslate. The only essence they need is &aInferium&r, so you can make them as soon as your Infusion Altar is up.",
    "",
    "If you want infinite building materials, these are a must!",
  ],
  "task.2C094D5DB8C21CE4.title": "Any Budding GeOre",
  "task.7BDA947BA827FC73.title": "Any GeOre Shard",
  "quest.33AC3264C0AE8FF1.title": "&fGrowing &bMobs",
  "quest.68A9B5BD25E86D75.title": "&cTertium Essence",
  "task.2CA99A333EDFB6FC.title": "&aEssence Farmlands",
  "quest.2F74CE4932170B99.quest_desc": [
    "When given &aHoney Treats&r, these will lure in either Yellow Carpenter Bees or Resin Bees.",
  ],
  "quest.37733B382007E7FA.quest_desc": [
    "Plenty of bees in this pack make materials from other mods. JEI lists how each one is made, and it is usually one of three routes.",
    "",
    "- &aBreeding&r: two parents and their flowers, like the vanilla material bees.",
    "- &aConversion&r: feed a bee a specific item and it turns into another type.",
    "- &aMachine recipes&r: other bees' spawn eggs go through another mod's machine, such as an &eEnder IO&r Alloy Smelter or a &eMystical Agriculture&r Infusion Altar.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Machine recipes are why spawn eggs matter. You make them in a &aBaBee Incubator&r from an egg and a Honey Treat carrying that bee's type gene.",
    "",
    "Each of these bees still needs its flower near the hive before it makes anything. For many of them that flower is a block of the material it produces, such as a Soularium Block for the Soularium Bee.",
  ],
  "quest.580DDEAC95562B05.title": "&bTier 4 &rSeeds",
  "quest.39FB54DD235A1E10.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSlimy Nest&r will lure in Slimy Bees by using Honey Treats when placed in a swamp biome.",
  ],
  "quest.780FEFE9F073543B.quest_desc": [
    "&eNautec&r has a resource farm of its own, grown from bacteria. Every strain makes one item, from stone up to iron and gold ingots, and a colony set in a &2Bio Reactor&r keeps making it for as long as the reactor has power.",
    "",
    "Your first colony is grafted off a block such as stone in an ocean or sand on a beach, then mutated toward the strain you want. Making items doesn't use the colony up, and a colony kept fed from the reactor's nutrient slots doesn't age either.",
    "",
    "The quests next to this one are linked from the &eNautec&r chapter, so finishing them here or there counts for both.",
  ],
  "quest.147C1793BE9C2766.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBaBee Incubator&r is used to speed up the process of aging for baby bees. To do this, insert 20 Honey Treats, a captured baby bee, and power to start the process.",
    "",
    "This can also be used to convert eggs into &bBee Spawn Eggs&r by infusing them with the genes from the bee you'd like to create.",
  ],
  "quest.5CE002C1C1142CD1.quest_desc": [
    "To craft any usable seeds for resources, we'll need to make an &aInfusion Altar&r and 8 &2Infusion Pedestals&r.",
    "",
    "Placing the &aAltar&r down will show you the location of the 8 surrounding &2Pedestals&r.",
    "",
    "You'll need a &aProsperity Seed Base&r to craft most of the resource seeds in the mod, aside from &9Mob Seeds&r.",
    "",
    "To craft them, place the items needed on each Pedestal and then give the &aAltar&r a redstone signal to start. You can also place a &cBlock of Redstone&r under the &aAltar&r to instantly start any valid recipes.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The items do not have to follow any order when placed on the Pedestals.",
  ],
  "quest.603BAFEF92DA275E.title": "&aInferium &rArmor",
  "task.27FFF0492348277F.title": "&dGrowth Accelerators",
  "quest.12FF1650CEA4083D.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Centrifuge",
  "quest.4506DB8F74B9C6A7.title": "&5The Altarnators",
  "quest.7C4F7E36320797C5.title": "&bTier 4 &rMob Seeds",
  "task.5F91F645D55E49BB.title": "Any &2Tier 2 &rSeeds",
  "quest.702D49883F3011DE.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSeed Reprocessor&r breaks a seed down into 2 of its crop's essence.",
    "",
    "Crops planted in the world only give back the seed you planted in this pack, so a field never makes spares. &eAgritech Evolved&r planters do return an extra seed 20% of the time. The Reprocessor is where those spares go, along with seeds you are done with.",
  ],
  "quest.283BBAFACC4EABB0.quest_desc": [
    "The &aMining Portal&r opens a flat world made for digging. Under a grass surface sit 64 layers of stone and 64 of deepslate, with ore veins spread all the way down to bedrock.",
    "",
    "Along with the vanilla ores it carries most of the pack's modded ones, &6Adamantite&r included.",
    "",
    "It only works in the Overworld. Place it at your base and use it to travel, and the dimension builds a matching portal where you land for the trip home.",
  ],
  "quest.5E04779BC1EB52E9.title": "&bElemental Seeds",
  "quest.51729919E9A33049.title": "&fBee Genes",
  "quest.40D416328C50C9F4.quest_desc": [
    "Coal geodes turn up about once every 60 chunks and iron about once every 120. Redstone is the rarest of this group at about once every 240.",
    "",
    "An iron shard smelts into one iron ingot, and JEI shows what the other shards turn into.",
  ],
  "quest.1003322F319665FF.title": "&cThe Wither",
  "quest.10AE11528D94EB0E.quest_desc": [
    "&eMystical Agriculture&r and &eMystical Automation&r have their own set of machines for automation and quality of life.",
    "",
    "These burn furnace fuels into an internal buffer and have an upgrade slot for a &2Machine Upgrade&r. A higher tier &2upgrade&r makes the machine run faster and holds more fuel, but it burns that fuel faster too.",
    "",
    "The &aTinkering Table&r and &2Enchanter&r are grouped here as well, but they need no frame and no fuel.",
  ],
  "quest.1ED979557DB19A2D.title": "&aEmerald Bees",
  "quest.1ED979557DB19A2D.quest_desc": [
    "With Diamond Bees, we can finally make the &6Emerald Bee&r!",
    "",
    "To make one, breed a Diamond Bee with a &aSlimy Bee&r.",
  ],
  "quest.7885F26DBF1E2E8F.title": "&dPassing Traits On",
  "quest.2315DBE189D330DA.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Productivity Omega",
  "quest.580DDEAC95562B05.quest_desc": [
    "&2Imperium&r opens the fourth tier, with seeds such as Gold, Lapis Lazuli and Experience.",
    "",
    "Every seed in this tier takes Imperium Essence worth 256 Inferium Essence, so automate the Inferium side before you work through the whole tier.",
  ],
  "quest.34C57701B6B07948.title": "&eGeOre",
  "quest.7695C03E7A574D93.quest_desc": [
    "&bProsperity Shards&r are mined from Prosperity ore. You'll need a lot of this to make the different seeds in Mystical Ag. It's also used in making most of the tools and armor.",
    "",
    "One of the most important uses is to make the &aInferium Crystal&r. This Crystal will upgrade 4 essences into the next tier, starting with Inferium. Every tier above that has its own crystal.",
    "",
    "Eventually, you can make a Crystal that never breaks, but it's probably a good idea to make a few of these.",
  ],
  "quest.39FB54DD235A1E10.title": "&fSlimy Nest",
  "quest.0C259021A652EFCE.title": "&aSpeeding Up Farms &rwith Blocks!",
  "quest.611514BAC644DA7A.quest_desc": [
    "A &aTrader&r holds one villager and lets you trade with it right there. The &3Auto Trader&r runs one of its trades by itself from the items you feed it.",
  ],
  "quest.7123022757E50A70.quest_desc": [
    "This is the max tier essence for seed crafting. &5Insanium&r seeds require a &6Crux&r to be able to grow. These are placed directly below the farmland.",
    "",
    "1 Insanium = 1,024 Inferium Essence",
  ],
  "quest.12FF1650CEA4083D.quest_desc": [
    "Raw combs still need a trip through a centrifuge. The &aCentrifuge Upgrade&r spins every comb as soon as a bee makes it, so the Storage fills with the finished products and their fluids instead.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aCentrifuge Upgrade&r and put it in the Controller. It replaces a bank of &2Heated Centrifuges&r and all the piping between them.",
    "",
    "At this tier it gives what a centrifuge would. Combs with no centrifuge recipe come out unchanged.",
  ],
  "task.4F1777D10DAD6649.title": "Any &bElemental &rSeed",
  "quest.7C4F7E36320797C5.quest_desc": [
    "Mob seeds at &2Imperium&r, for drops the earlier tiers cannot reach.",
    "",
    "Each seed still takes four filled Soul Jars of its mob. A basic &2Soulium Dagger&r adds one soul per kill and these jars need 4 to 10 souls each, so expect a proper hunt, or feed the mob's drops to a &aSoul Extractor&r.",
  ],
  "quest.0A1FDABEAAA0723B.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Simulator",
  "quest.2436337445AD0E07.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Block",
  "quest.4B38B74EA8E13AAE.title": "&eMob Flow Utilities",
  "quest.3F89BB2A4D278D16.quest_desc": [
    "The Simulator keeps bees inside one hive. The &eMystian Apiary&r takes that further and runs up to 108 caged bees inside a single 3x3x3 block, with none of them ever flying off.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aApiary Controller&r and the three boxes it runs, then build the apiary. Each bee makes a batch every 3,840 ticks (3.2 minutes) before upgrades, and its flower never has to be in range.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The apiary is a 3x3x3 cube with a &2Honeycomb Block&r in the middle.",
    "",
    "The four boxes go on the four sides of the Honeycomb Block, one of each, in any order. Every other block in the cube is a log or wood block, stripped or not. The log straight above the Honeycomb Block can be swapped for a second &aApiary Storage&r.",
    "",
    "{image:ftb:textures/quests/productivebees/mystian_apiary.png width:120 height:135 align:center click_action:none:}",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Put filled &2Bee Cages&r in the Bee Box and one of each flower or block your bees need in the Flower Box. Flowers are never used up.",
    "",
    "Everything the bees make goes into the Storage. When it fills up, the bees wait until there is room again, so nothing is lost.",
    "",
    "The Controller holds the upgrades. Speed, Productivity and Gene Sampler upgrades stack up to four each, and it also takes a Block upgrade and the apiary's own Centrifuge Upgrade.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the Controller only takes the basic &2Speed Upgrade&r. Speed II won't go in its slot.",
  ],
  "quest.458B3C345767E296.title": "&5Nether Star Seeds",
  "quest.72D582D05DC9C7A2.title": "&fOak Nest",
  "quest.63E02402233F6865.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBreeding Chamber&r allows you to breed bees all in one block!",
    "",
    "Place in two &bcaged bees&r that you want to breed together, supply them each with their preferred breeding flower, and then put some empty &bBee Cages&r for the new baby bee to be captured in. You'll also need to supply the chamber with power to function!",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Some bees can create several types of bees, so if you are aiming to make one of those specific types, just pick up and place one of the parent bees back in until it shows the bee you are looking for as the outcome!",
    "",
    "This machine can also be upgraded with speed upgrades to be faster.",
  ],
  "quest.16C668B00B581A9C.title": "&fBee Types",
  "quest.562421EC1575F837.quest_desc": [
    "Once you have a &aCrystalline Bee&r and an &2Ashy Mining Bee&r, you can breed them together to make an Iron Bee!",
  ],
  "quest.3F89BB2A4D278D16.title": "&eMystian Apiary",
  "task.0ADB488118F04CF5.title": "Bee Stats",
  "quest.34C57701B6B07948.quest_desc": [
    "&eGeOre&r adds geodes for common ores next to vanilla's amethyst ones. In the Overworld they generate from y=-58 up to y=30. Coal geodes are the most common and emerald the rarest.",
    "",
    "Break a cluster by hand for 2 &aShards&r, or with a pickaxe for 4 plus Fortune. Budding blocks drop nothing when broken, so farm them where you find them.",
  ],
  "quest.358D66AB9176F05F.title": "&aHands-Free Shards",
  "quest.20ED9BF15D0E7F54.quest_desc": [
    "Each tier of the &aCentrifuge Upgrade&r multiplies what a comb gives. Tier 1 doubles it, Tier 2 triples it, and Tier 3 gives four times the normal output.",
    "",
    "Raise your &aCentrifuge Upgrade&r to Tier 3. Each tier is crafted from the one before, so you work through all of them.",
    "",
    "Combs with no centrifuge recipe are never multiplied.",
  ],
  "quest.5574D291E6E69013.quest_desc": [
    "1 Prudentium = 4 Inferium Essence",
  ],
  "quest.5C2FD440426A2BD7.quest_desc": [
    "&eAgritech&r planters can grow &eMystical Agriculture&r seeds.",
    "",
    "Agritech has planter recipes for the standard Mystical Agriculture and Agradditions seeds, but not for this pack's extra crops such as Desh. Drop an essence seed into a planter on the right soil and it grows like any other crop.",
    "",
    "&cThe soil has to match the seed's tier&r, so &2Essence Farmland&r grows its own tier and everything below it; &aTertium Farmland&r covers tiers 1 through 3 and &dSupremium Farmland&r covers everything except &5Insanium&r tier seeds, which need their &6Crux&r in the soil slot instead of farmland.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[ \"Everything you build in the \", { \"text\": \"Agritech Questline\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"15441C87BEDC510C\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"value\": {\"translate\": \"Go to Agritech Questline\"}, \"action\": \"show_text\"} }, \" over in the Cooking and Brewing chapter applies to your essence farm too. \", {\"text\": \"Infused Farmland\", \"color\": \"dark_green\"}, \" counts as soil for every tier below Insanium, and \", {\"text\": \"Cloche Domes\", \"color\": \"green\"}, \", the \", {\"text\": \"Fertilizer Spreader\", \"color\": \"dark_green\"}, \" and the \", {\"text\": \"Silo\", \"color\": \"green\"}, \" work on essence planters like any other.\" ]",
  ],
  "quest.67F07FBB50AB431F.title": "&aSpawner Farms",
  "quest.34F054E75A7CAD47.title": "&aHarvester \\&\\ Fertilizer",
  "quest.7CB0AFF443CB39DA.quest_desc": [
    "The &aEnchanter&r applies a chosen enchantment without spending any XP levels. Load two ingredients into its input slots and a tool or a plain &aBook&r into the item slot to enchant that item.",
    "",
    "The level of the enchantment depends on how many items you use. Each level costs the full ingredient amount again, so a fifth level takes five times what the first one does. It stops at the enchantment's normal maximum. It gives no result for an item that already carries a different enchantment that could sit alongside this one, so enchant a plain Book or an unenchanted tool.",
    "",
    "The &aEnchanternator&r runs Enchanter recipes on its own at a level you pick, using furnace fuel.",
  ],
  "quest.34C9EDD591FC72AC.title": "&aUnbeelievable Upgrades",
  "quest.5FB291FDE43A727F.quest_desc": [
    "&aHoney Treats&r have a ton of uses in &eProductive Bees&r. They lure bees into nests, heal and calm bees, carry genes, and go into the Upgrade Base that hive upgrades are built on.",
    "",
    "&aBee Cages&r let you pick up a bee and carry it around. A plain Bee Cage is used up when you let the bee out, while a &aSturdy Bee Cage&r comes back empty every time. Sturdy ones turn up in village chests, and &dThe Apiarist&r sells them too.",
  ],
  "quest.34C9EDD591FC72AC.quest_desc": [
    "There are several upgrades that you can use to make your &2Productive Bee&r journey better!",
    "",
    "All of them require the &aUpgrade Base&r to craft, so might as well make a bunch of Honey Treats!",
    "",
    "An Advanced Beehive only takes upgrades once an Expansion Box is attached to any side except the front. Break the box and the upgrades drop out.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: There are several upgrades that don't have a quest. You can always check them out in JEI!",
  ],
  "quest.10B7437F3E412D26.title": "&7Ancient Bees",
  "quest.40D416328C50C9F4.title": "&fCommon GeOres",
  "quest.0241EAE68EA53595.quest_desc": [
    "Lots of Bees can be found by crafting &2Nests&r!",
    "",
    "Most &2Nests&r require an item to be used on them to lure bees, with the basic nests requiring &aHoney Treats&r. Using one will start the timer for a bee to come move in, and using more will cut the time needed for them to spawn in.",
  ],
  "quest.2AE9ADF578ABEA11.title": "&dSupremium Essence",
  "quest.6AB0C61A12C417F2.title": "&cSoulium Spawner",
  "quest.0EBA58B7FD2AF36D.title": "&aExtracting Unique Materials",
  "quest.290D1B111FD24B32.title": "&bDiamond Bees",
  "quest.5C2FD440426A2BD7.title": "&eAgritech&r meets &eMystical Agriculture",
  "quest.51B5EE931AC1B86E.title": "&cNether &rNests",
  "quest.283BBAFACC4EABB0.title": "&bMining Dimension",
  "quest.792BD1143635482C.quest_desc": [
    "These Nests must be placed in certain types of biomes to lure bees!",
    "",
    "&aGravel Nests&r must be placed in a river or beach biome to lure in bees. Using Honey Treats can lure in Ashy Mining, Chocolate Mining, and Digger bees.",
    "",
    "&aSand Nests&r must be placed in a sandy biome such as a desert, badlands or beach. Using Honey Treats will lure Chocolate or Ashy Mining bees.",
  ],
  "quest.197CF94F783E59DF.title": "&aUpgrade&r: Speed",
  "task.7FF1BA8529B79913.title": "Centrifuges",
  "quest.66477F0AB0AC2CDB.title": "&aCrafter",
  "task.0C41CFCD491848EC.title": "&aInferium &rArmor",
  "quest.1A4F6C1AC9BD2F42.title": "&cRedstone Bees",
  "quest.6451DEA471C5FF6F.title": "&aDamage Pads",
  "quest.1D4A7C29E5B30F16.quest_desc": [
    "&eDimensional Resources&r puts new planets in the sky and gives you a &2laser&r to mine them from the ground.",
    "",
    "To get started, find &2Dimensional Ore&r deep underground, between y=-64 and y=-16. Mining it drops the &aDimensional Shard Gems&r that every part of the mod is built from.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Hold the GuideMe key \", \"color\": \"gray\", \"italic\": true}, {\"keybind\": \"key.guideme.guide\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: G\"}}, {\"text\": \" on the laser or a Planet Locator, or open the \", \"color\": \"gray\", \"italic\": true}, {\"text\": \"full illustrated guide\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"italic\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,dimresources:guide,dimresources:index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Dimensional Resources Guide\"}}]",
  ],
  "quest.2D2EC0BCFF1DA68C.quest_desc": [
    "When captured in a Bee Cage, most bees will show specific stats. Let's go over those!",
    "",
    "&aProductivity&r: Determines the amount of combs produced, with the highest stat being &6Very High&r.",
    "",
    "&aWeather Tolerance&r: Determines if the bee can work in certain weather conditions, with &6Any&r being the best.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&aBehavior&r: Determines what kind of shift the bee likes to work. Diurnal meaning during the day, Nocturnal meaning during the night. The best type is &6Metaturnal&r, which makes the bee work no matter what time of day it is.",
    "",
    "&aEndurance&r: Decides whether the bee survives after stinging something. A &6Strong&r bee always does, and a Medium bee does half the time.",
    "",
    "&aTemper&r: How the bee treats you. Aggressive bees go after nearby players without being provoked, and &6Passive&r bees never get angry at all.",
    "",
    "This tooltip will also show you the items needed for it to breed!",
  ],
  "quest.60EBD67EDCE669DD.title": "&dTier 5 &rSeeds",
  "quest.5010FC8F326DE471.quest_desc": [
    "&eMystical Agriculture&r gear takes &dAugments&r, and the &aTinkering Table&r is where you fit them. Put the tool or armor piece in the center slot and augments in the slots to its right.",
    "",
    "Augments start as a &aBlank Augment&r and are made on the &bInfusion Altar&r. An augment only fits the kind of gear it is made for, and only gear of its own tier or higher. Most gear holds one augment, while Awakened Supremium gear holds two.",
    "",
    "Taking an augment back out of the table removes it from the gear, so you can swap them whenever you like.",
  ],
  "quest.208A53545D649C8D.title": "&aMachine Upgrades",
  "quest.09BC75B655BDC624.quest_desc": [
    "Breeding the same type of bee over and over by hand gets tedious. That's where the &aBaBee Upgrade&r comes in!",
    "",
    "Each one installed in an Advanced Beehive adds a 5% chance for a baby bee to pop out whenever an adult bee leaves after dropping off honey. The baby comes from breeding that bee with another bee in the hive, and nothing spawns once 10 or more bees are within 5 blocks.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It does nothing for bees that can't breed with their own kind, such as Skeletal Bees and Withered Bees, or for bees that need a special breeding item instead of flowers, such as &dDraconic Bees&r. A caged bee's tooltip shows both.",
    "",
    "This can also be used as a filter in the &aCatcher&r to allow it to only capture baby bees!",
  ],
  "quest.3738420663297397.title": "&aKeeping The Lights Out",
  "quest.1CFEC4265CAAA0D8.title": "&aInferium &rWatering Can",
  "quest.5E04779BC1EB52E9.quest_desc": [
    "The &bElemental Seeds&r are used to make some of the basic elements, like providing recipes for Water and Lava buckets.",
    "",
    "Their essences also fill the &2Essence Vessels&r around the &aAwakening Altar&r, which is how you make Awakened Supremium.",
  ],
  "quest.1DBAC590575ABA64.title": "&dDebris Geodes",
  "quest.34F054E75A7CAD47.quest_desc": [
    "Both machines cover the 3x3 patch directly in front, with each upgrade tier widening that range by two blocks, up to 15x15 with an &6Awakened Supremium Upgrade&r. They check one block per cycle, so a larger field requires better upgrades.",
    "",
    "- &aFertilizer&r: Uses &#e5a2dcFertilized Essence&r and similar items to grow crops in front of it.",
    "- &2Harvester&r: Harvests fully grown crops, then uses one seed from each harvest to replant and sends everything else in its output slots.",
    "",
    "The &aFertilizer&r only works on crops planted in the world. It does nothing for machines like a Farmer, which grow crops inside itself.",
  ],
  "task.3D6DD528D310D8B9.title": "Any &bTier 4 &rMob Seeds",
  "quest.3F8B2D61C4A97E05.title": "&bReading the Sky",
}